From b1a4b45b754f4c4fe9679891c0cf962fb6c74f11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeff R. Day" <phroun@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SDL host: fix solo restore, harden zero-size compositing,
 drop SDL2 stragglers

Three graphical-host fixes, plus a cleanup left from the SDL3 migration.

1. Solo maximize -> restore reconfigures the swapchain. In solo mode the app
   is the primary OS window (created RESIZABLE, its border stripped at
   runtime); a torn window is borderless from birth. Restoring the solo
   window from zoom-to-fill left the GPU swapchain at the maximized size, so
   the restored content painted into its top-left corner and the stale frame
   stayed on screen until a manual edge-drag. SetScreenSizePx now clears an
   OS MAXIMIZED flag before resizing (SetWindowSize no-ops on a maximized
   window) and drives the framebuffer reconfigure from the window's actual
   pixel size instead of waiting on a WINDOW_RESIZED that a programmatic
   resize did not reliably deliver. Both are idempotent (liveResize no-ops
   when the backend already matches) and reuse the same
   Resized -> SetBounds -> onResize chain every OS resize already runs, so
   no new recursion. Adds sdl3.WINDOW_MAXIMIZED and Window.SizeInPixels().

2. Compositing tolerates a collapsed host. Dragging the desktop window to a
   near-zero height with a child window or overlay open panicked:
   "image: NewRGBA Rectangle has huge or negative dimensions". The compositor
   derives a per-unit pixel scale as hostPixels/hostUnits; core.Unit is an
   int, so a far-enough shrink rounds the host unit extent to 0, float64(n)/0
   is +Inf, and int(math.Round(+Inf)) is MaxInt64, which NewScaled rejects.
   The existing guards checked the (huge, positive) result. Guard the divisor
   instead in RenderFrameWithChildWindows and drawOverlay, matching the
   frame-level scale that was already guarded; there is nothing to composite
   onto at zero area, so the child is skipped and the overlay bails (its
   callers already skip on error).

3. Drop straggling SDL2 references. buildwin.sh still cross-built for Windows
   the SDL2 way (CGO, MinGW, a vendored SDL2 statically linked). SDL3 and the
   WebGPU native library are bound through purego/goffi and opened at run
   time, so the Windows build is a plain CGO-free `GOOS=windows go build`
   with the sdlembed tag bundling SDL3; the script is rewritten to that. Code
   comments that still called the running system SDL2 are corrected to SDL3
   or version-neutral wording. compositing-handoff.md is left as-is: it
   accurately narrates the SDL2 -> SDL3 migration itself.

Build 16. Builds and vets standalone (plain and -tags "sdl webgpu"); the
sdl and raster suites pass with no mew module in the graph.
